## 4b.  DUPLICATE KEY GUARD
##      A Python dict literal silently keeps only the LAST occurrence
##      of a repeated key -- MODERN_TECH_SKILLS is written as a
##      literal, so any accidental repeat of a canonical name silently
##      drops the earlier definition (and its aliases) with no error
##      and no warning. This scans this file's own source text for
##      repeated "Name": ( keys inside MODERN_TECH_SKILLS and fails
##      loud instead of failing silent, so a future accidental repeat
##      gets caught immediately instead of quietly losing data.
