#This script is NOT part of the runtime parser — it is a build-time tool.
#
#Usage:
#    python build_skills_taxonomy.py --onet Software_Skills.txt --output data/skills_taxonomy.json
#
#What it does:
#    1. Reads the O*NET Software Skills TSV file
#    2. Keeps only tech-relevant categories (drops medical, legal, CAD, etc.)
#    3. Always keeps O*NET "Hot Technology" flagged skills regardless of category
#    4. Auto-generates aliases for each skill (lowercase, punctuation variants)
#    5. Merges a hand-curated MODERN_TECH_SKILLS block (AWS, GCP, RAG, BERT, etc.)
#       that O*NET does not yet cover
#    6. Writes the final taxonomy as JSON
#
#Output format (one entry per canonical skill):
#    {
#        "Python": {
#            "aliases": ["python3", "python 3", "py"],
#            "category": "programming_language",
#            "source": "custom"         ← or "onet" or "onet_hot"
#        },
#        ...
#    }
